# NOTE ON COMMENTS IN THIS FILE. This file is TRACKED and PUBLIC. Every comment here ships.
# A path tells a reader that something is ignored, which is unavoidable and low-information.
# A comment describing WHAT a file contains, how severe it is, or whether it is still open is
# high-information and defeats the point of ignoring it. Keep entries below content-free.

# Cloned upstream repos kept as read-only reference (~5 GB, each has its own .git) — ignored,
# but the upstream-URL + pinned-commit manifest IS tracked so the refs are reproducible.
reference/*
!reference/MANIFEST.md
# rubicon is NOT a cloned repo — it's small, curated, explorer-fetched verified source the
# 8x-01 docs depend on (provenance in its README + file headers). Tracked as an exception.
!reference/rubicon/

# The Zipcode UI lives in its own repo (resi-labs-ai/zipcode-finance-euler); this monorepo's
# frontend/ is a local dev scratch dir only, not part of the public repo.
frontend/

# subgraph/ is empty scaffolding, not yet real — kept local until there's something to publish.
subgraph/

# docs-site/ duplicates published docs living elsewhere — not part of this repo.
docs-site/

# Security working directories. Local only, by decision.
audit/
adversarial-review/
build/

# Bridge working directory. Local only, by decision.
bridge/

# Foundry build artifacts
contracts/out/
contracts/cache/
contracts/broadcast/

# Local env / secrets (the .example template stays tracked)
.env
*.env
!.env.example
!*.env.example
contracts/.env

# Working notes and internal planning. Local only, by decision. No leading slash, so these match
# at any depth and are caught wherever the file is dropped.
*-analysis.md
*-analysis*.md
FUCK_UR_MOM.md
fable.md
carry-risk.md

# Local only, by decision. LOCAL-ONLY MEANS ONE DISK: no private-repo copy of these exists, and
# their cited sources are memory files that do not either. Back them up out-of-band.
DISPOSITIONS.md
CLAUDE.md
